{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/pulls/4","id":4086487317,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTZUlPc7zktkV","html_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback/seer/pull/4","diff_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback/seer/pull/4.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback/seer/pull/4.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kristofferremback/seer/issues/4","number":4,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"S3 blob store: zips and images in S3, boot-time disk migration","user":{"login":"kristofferremback","id":9280031,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODAwMzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9280031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback","html_url":"https://github.com/kristofferremback","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kristofferremback/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nMoves all blob storage (bundle zips + uploaded images) off the local volume and into S3, making the app stateless apart from SQLite (users, workspaces, keys, metadata) and the disposable extraction cache.\n\n- **Store** (`src/store.ts`): dual backend behind the same API — `S3_BUCKET` set → Bun's native `S3Client`; unset → disk exactly as before (local dev, tests). Keys mirror the disk layout: `zips/<ws>/<slug>/<version>.zip`, `images/<ws>/<img_id>`.\n- **Serving is unchanged from the outside**: images stream through Seer (`s3file.stream()`, never `new Response(s3file)` which would redirect to a presigned AWS URL — access control stays ours); zips are fetched from S3 into the existing extraction cache with the same TTL/sweep. No endpoint or URL diffs, image compression untouched.\n- **One-time migration** (`src/migrate-blobs.ts`): at boot, before the server binds, every blob recorded in SQLite is copied to S3. Idempotent (skips objects already present at the right size), marker-gated via `meta.blob_store`, crash-safe re-entry, fails the boot loudly if a blob is missing from both stores. Local files are left in place as a safety net.\n- **Config**: `S3_BUCKET`, `S3_REGION` (or `S3_ENDPOINT`), `S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` (AWS_* aliases accepted); misconfiguration fails at boot. `startServer()` is now async so a failed migration exits non-zero instead of lingering.\n\n## Infra (already provisioned)\n\n- Private bucket `seer-build-982750043547` (eu-north-1, public access fully blocked)\n- IAM user `seer-app` with an inline policy scoped to only that bucket (List/Get/Put/Delete)\n- Railway variables staged on the `seer` service (`--skip-deploys`): the migration runs on the first deploy of this branch's merge\n\n## Testing\n\n- 110 tests pass (`bun test`), typecheck clean\n- Live end-to-end against the real bucket: seeded a bundle + image in disk mode → restarted with S3 → boot migration uploaded both → pages and images served from S3 → new uploads (bundle v2 + second image) landed in S3 only, nothing new on disk → third restart confirmed the migration is a marker-gated no-op\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-07-19T16:42:03Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T18:20:07Z","closed_at":"2026-07-19T16:42:12Z","merged_at":"2026-07-19T16:42:12Z","merge_commit_sha":"1fd55e121dfd39615018a840375611d900e7409b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers"